    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8ee5e62a_a16330de",
        "filename": "common/build.mk",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 160,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000768
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-09-12T20:30:09Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "why this indirection ?  why not depend on $(TOUCHPAD_FW) directly ?",
      "revId": "ce87c1129c1f640d0bf420c73514b10a76bffe4f",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a74774b9_68fd2754",
        "filename": "common/build.mk",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 160,
      "author": {
        "id": 1129199
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-09-13T06:15:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "To avoid recomputing the hash (and therefore the object file, and EC image) on every single build (see the .PHONY logic below), and yet force rebuild when TOUCHPAD_FW parameter is changed.",
      "parentUuid": "8ee5e62a_a16330de",
      "revId": "ce87c1129c1f640d0bf420c73514b10a76bffe4f",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c76e05c3_ccf96a18",
        "filename": "common/build.mk",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 160,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000768
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-09-13T07:01:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "TOUCHPAD_FW is a path to an external file that doesn\u0027t change when you run `make`.  so why would the hash need to be recalculated when TOUCHPAD_FW doesn\u0027t change ?  make would see that the generated header file is newer than the TOUCHPAD_FW source and thus skip it.\n\nif i\u0027m reading this code correctly, the hash gets updated only when the *path* to the firmware file changes, not when the firmware file itself changes.  that doesn\u0027t make sense.",
      "parentUuid": "a74774b9_68fd2754",
      "revId": "ce87c1129c1f640d0bf420c73514b10a76bffe4f",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0b20f719_02a9dad4",
        "filename": "common/build.mk",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 160,
      "author": {
        "id": 1129199
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-09-13T08:40:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So, if you replace this whole block by:\n\n$(out)/touchpad_fw_hash.h: $(out)/util/gen_touchpad_hash $(TOUCHPAD_FW)\n\t$(call quiet,tp_hash,TPHASH )\n\nDoing this:\nmake BOARD\u003dhammer -j\n(pass no touchpad firwmare)\nthen\nmake TOUCHPAD_FW\u003dSA459C-1211_ForGoogleHammer_4.0.bin BOARD\u003dhammer -j\n\ndoes not force hashes to be recomputed (because SA459C-1211_ForGoogleHammer_4.0.bin modification time is older than build/hammer/touchpad_fw_hash.h). You have to manually \"touch SA459C-1211_ForGoogleHammer_4.0.bin\" to force a rebuild. We want to avoid that (for developer convenience mostly).\n\n\u003e if i\u0027m reading this code correctly, the hash gets updated only when the *path* to the firmware file changes, not when the firmware file itself changes.  that doesn\u0027t make sense.\n\nWell, we are suffering from a similar issue as above, but if the path does not change, and $(TOUCHPAD_FW) is more recent than .touchpad_fw, the hashes will be rebuild.",
      "parentUuid": "c76e05c3_ccf96a18",
      "revId": "ce87c1129c1f640d0bf420c73514b10a76bffe4f",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c0ea9a03_143a1e75",
        "filename": "common/build.mk",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 160,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000768
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-09-13T14:34:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "so it isn\u0027t that my suggestion would force a rebuild every time, it\u0027s that your code is working around one limitation and introducing a different limitation ;).  this deserves a comment.\n\nyou can address the timestamp issue by changing the echo to a ls:\n\n @ls -l \"$(TOUCHPAD_FW)\" \u003e $@",
      "parentUuid": "0b20f719_02a9dad4",
      "revId": "ce87c1129c1f640d0bf420c73514b10a76bffe4f",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
